  "description_short": "Beachfront seafood and pub grub with sunset views over Plett's Central Beach.",
  "description_long": "Moby's sits right on Central Beach in Plettenberg Bay, where the sound of waves mixes with the buzz of a busy beachfront pub. The location is hard to beat—wooden decks overlook the sand, and sunset here turns the sea gold. It's the kind of place where you kick off your sandals after a beach day and settle in with a cold beer.\n\nThe menu covers seafood staples like fish and chips, calamari, and prawns, alongside burgers and steaks for those who prefer to stay on dry land. Portions are generous, prices are fair, and the vibe is relaxed and unpretentious. Families, surfers, and holidaymakers all find their way here, drawn by the view and the easygoing atmosphere.\n\nService can be slower when it's packed, especially over summer holidays, but the setting makes up for it. Whether you're here for a lazy lunch or sundowners with your toes in the sand, Moby's delivers that classic Plett beach experience without any fuss.",
